Run Skia on GL when it cannot make a Vulkan GrContext, and keep GPU channel
retries from spinning.

Split out of ohos-gpu-startup-diagnostics.patch once the diagnosis it was
written for was done; its step-by-step start-up logging is gone.

On the 2in1 emulator (Vulkan 1.1 translated from the host's GPU) Skia's
Vulkan GrContext failed although the instance, device queue and context
provider came up. It failed only when the first channel asked for a shared
context, long after the GPU process told the browser it was up, so the
process refused every channel and the window stayed black. On OHOS the GPU
service now asks Skia for a GrContext as soon as the Vulkan context provider
exists; if Skia says no it drops the provider, runs Skia on GL and reports
Vulkan disabled, and the browser records the GPU mode as GL. GpuServiceImpl's
preferences and feature info stop being const on OHOS for it. When Skia does
fail, the context provider says what it was given -- versions, allocator,
extensions, and any function Skia requires that cannot be found -- which a
tablet's Vulkan will need.

A failed channel is asked for again after a growing pause (100 ms more each
time, at most 2 s) instead of at once, dozens of times a second, for as long
as the app runs.

And the GPU process's own log reaches hilog again: VizMainImpl replaces the
handler that wrote it there with one that forwards it to the browser for
chrome://gpu, so the browser writes what it is forwarded, WARNING and above,
as "OHOS GPU process says:".

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch,
ohos-gpu-lose-context-debug-url.patch and
ohos-vulkan-compositor-diagnostics.patch.

